<section class="alt" id="how">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2>Five phases,<br>evidence-led throughout.</h2>
      <span class="label">How we implement</span>
    </div>
    <p class="section-intro">A 12-month, overlapping implementation. Co-design, build, localisation and capacity transfer run in parallel to compress the schedule. Each phase produces a decision point for the Steering Group before the next begins.</p>
    <ol class="phases">
      <li><span class="when">M1–3</span><h4>Co-design &amp; governance</h4><p>Steering group, pilot scope, legal alignment, content priorities.</p></li>
      <li><span class="when">M2–5</span><h4>Content &amp; platform build</h4><p>Iterative content, app and dashboard build, data governance.</p></li>
      <li><span class="when">M6–8</span><h4>Pilot implementation</h4><p>Selected cohorts use learning, assessment and reporting; trained trainers.</p></li>
      <li><span class="when">M8–10</span><h4>Evaluation &amp; refinement</h4><p>Analyse use data and feedback; adjust content and thresholds.</p></li>
      <li><span class="when">M10–12</span><h4>Rollout &amp; handover</h4><p>Scaling model, train-the-trainer, communications, ownership transfer.</p></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="governance">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2>Government-led, with<br>clear role separation.</h2>
      <span class="label">How it is governed</span>
    </div>
    <p class="section-intro">Ownership sits with government from day one. Delivery and evaluation are kept apart by design, so evidence on what works is generated independently of the party responsible for results.</p>
    <div class="govgrid">
      <div class="gov">
        <h4>Joint Steering Group</h4>
        <p>Chaired by the lead government agency, with ministries, agencies, training institutions and community representation. Confirms scope, owns decisions, validates milestones.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gov">
        <h4>Content governance</h4>
        <p>Defined review cycles, version control and alignment with national and international legal frameworks. Field observations feed back into improved modules.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gov">
        <h4>Independent evaluation</h4>
        <p>Monitoring, evaluation, accountability and learning (MEAL) is delivered by a partner with no implementation role, reporting findings directly to the Steering Group.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gov">
        <h4>Minimal, purposeful data</h4>
        <p>Only what is needed for training completion and licence readiness is collected, under access rules the government sets.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="authority-note"><b>Statutory authority preserved.</b> The platform supports training, documentation and readiness. It does not replace regulatory authority; approvals remain with the state.</div>
  </div>
</section>

